A patch to the runtime of OCaml 5.5.2 (runtime/afl.c). It lets an
AFL-instrumented OCaml program map the coverage bitmap that AFL++
passes as a POSIX shared memory descriptor in __AFL_SHM_FD, as AFL++
always does on macOS, keeping the SysV path (__AFL_SHM_ID); and it makes
the fork server speak the handshake of AFL++ 4.20c and later, which
reports the 64 KiB bitmap the OCaml instrumentation writes, where with
the old one afl-fuzz gives every instance an 8 MiB map. An afl-fuzz
older than 4.20c needs AFL_OLD_FORKSERVER=1 in the environment, as with
AFL++'s own runtime; without it the fork server stops at the first
execution and afl-fuzz reports that it could not request a process.

License: this patch modifies a file of the OCaml distribution and is
offered under that file's terms, LGPL-2.1-only with the OCaml static
linking exception (see LICENSE in the OCaml sources); it is not part of
typec and nothing in typec links it. Apply with patch -p1 in the OCaml
source tree; patch(1) ignores these lines.

